Subject: visionOS 3D: GE Plus's folder screens are flat, like every menu (D-055)

menuRender() draws every menu inside the flat span (D-055): identical in both
eyes, exactly on the panel. GE Plus's front end (gexfront.c, GoldenEye's own
folder screens) is handed over to BEFORE that span opens, and it draws the
folder as a model through its own camera and scale matrices - so in 3D the
fold took it for WORLD. Measured on the Vision Pro simulator over Multiplayer
Options: stereo_frame_world=7, stereo_frame_flat=0, the paper and folder at
+3 px disparity and the text (rectangles) at 0 px, i.e. the words floating a
little in front of the page they are printed on.

gexFrontRender() now runs inside a flat span of its own. The tags are G_NOOPs:
nothing changes in 2D or on any other platform, and the M-001 replay never
opens GE Plus.

GoldenEye's intro (geIntroRender, the gun barrel and cast reel) is left as it
is - a cinematic, which the fold treats as the world like Perfect Dark's own
cutscenes.

diff --git a/src/game/menu.c b/src/game/menu.c
index 604829745..9d6628d02 100644
--- a/src/game/menu.c
+++ b/src/game/menu.c
@@ -6056,7 +6056,14 @@ Gfx *menuRender(Gfx *gdl)
 
 		overfront = true;
 	} else if (gexFrontIsActive()) {
+		// GE Plus's folder screens are menus too (D-055's flat span), but they
+		// are drawn here, before the span below opens, through gexfront.c's own
+		// camera and scale matrices - so in 3D the folder was folded as WORLD
+		// (+3 px behind the panel) under its own text at 0 px. Flat, like
+		// every other menu.
+		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_BEGIN);
 		gdl = gexFrontRender(gdl);
+		gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_END);
 
 		if (!traceReportIsOpen()) {
 			return gdl;
